## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **1. Authentication approach**: The `users` table stores bcrypt-hashed passwords (from Laravel). Should I:
>    - **(a)** Build a simple session-based auth using cookies (recommended — matches the existing Laravel approach)?
>    - **(b)** Keep the demo role-switcher for now and skip auth entirely?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **2. Which phases should I prioritize?** I recommend this order:
>    - **Phase 6** (Real CRUD) first — this is the highest-impact change
>    - **Phase 11** (Global Search) — quick win, very useful
>    - **Phase 12** (Report Export) — straightforward
>    - **Phase 13** (Polish) — throughout
>    - **Phase 7** (Auth) — if you want real login
>    - **Phase 8–10** (Quotations, Endorsements, Renewals) — business logic features

> [!WARNING]
> **3. Data safety**: Once Phase 6 is live, the app will be able to create, update, and delete real records in your `vidhi_insurance` database. Should I add any safeguards (e.g., soft-delete instead of hard-delete, audit logs)?

